  "verdict": "Holistic classification reads a long packet in overlapping windows of pages. On packets of 30 to 60 pages with Claude Haiku 5.5, a 10-page window is a good place to start. It got the most sections exactly right, 67% against 62% with the default 20 pages, and cost 60% less: $39 against $103 of classification per 1,000 packets. The saving comes from pricing: a 20-page window with page images usually goes over 100,000 tokens, and Claude Haiku 5.5 charges more above that. A 15-page window cost about the same as 10 but got no more right than 20; a 40-page window cost the most. Test it on your own packets.",
